  "title": "Internal-state updates validate before applying while pool invariants remain mode-specific",
  "mechanism": "SchedulerInternalStateController validates every requested update before its apply loop and catches UpdateRejected only during validation. The apply loop can directly mutate worker state before a later handler fails; no rollback is shown. DFlash acceptance-threshold relaxation is rejected while an unfinished request carries a sampling mask, including running and PP batches, waiting and grammar queues, chunked requests, and decode preallocation, transfer, retracted and held-rebootstrap queues. The generic pool identity adds available, evictable, protected, session-held and uncached tokens. Hybrid-SSM total capacity comes from req_to_token_pool.schedulable_token_capacity. Page-interleaved sharding uses aggregate free pages and checks alignment; the separate legacy DCP branch tolerates a residual mismatch. SWA request-ring token conservation is skipped, and the request-pool check instead compares free slots plus session-held requests with size plus preallocation headroom.",
  "corrections": [
    "Validate-then-apply is not an atomic transaction.",
    "The sampling-mask function actually begins at line 255 and its final queue branches and predicate end at 282; the model review range 252-279 was still incomplete.",
    "Conservation exceptions are explicit mode conditions, not evidence that every residual represents a leak."
  ],
  "source_scope": "Manually read the listed exact Git ranges for the final corrected mechanism. All other model claims remain research notes; no runtime experiment.",
